# The root Makefile is Unix-only: a CR in a recipe breaks make. Scoped narrowly on purpose - the
# vendored third-party sources under Projects/ keep whatever line endings they ship with.
/Makefile text eol=lf

# The root automated-build script is Windows-only and needs CRLF. Scoped to the root (leading /) so
# any vendored .bat under Projects/ is left as it ships.
/BuildAll.bat text eol=crlf

# Its Unix counterpart: a CR breaks sh.
/BuildAll.sh text eol=lf
